{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00257",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.37,
      "end_seconds": 6.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Good afternoon. Take a seat, please. Alright, have you been waiting long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 6.85,
      "end_seconds": 9.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Yeah, only about ten minutes, no trouble."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.29,
      "end_seconds": 12.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Go ahead, tell me what's happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.14,
      "end_seconds": 24.3,
      "duration_seconds": 10.16,
      "text": "Um, mainly I've been wanting to stop smoking. That's why I came. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.1,
      "end_seconds": 29.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "What about cravings, mostly after meals, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.69,
      "end_seconds": 39.65,
      "duration_seconds": 9.96,
      "text": "Yeah. Two weeks, I'd say. Well, you know, about cravings, mostly after meals, pretty moderate, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.12,
      "end_seconds": 45.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "What about irritability when you try to cut down, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.8,
      "end_seconds": 48.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "Yes, I have."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.0,
      "end_seconds": 51.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Let me double-check something in your record."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.69,
      "end_seconds": 53.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Of course, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.64,
      "end_seconds": 67.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.31,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Any alcohol problems, coughing up blood, low mood or chest pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.41,
      "end_seconds": 71.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "No, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.69,
      "end_seconds": 76.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.35,
      "end_seconds": 79.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.67,
      "end_seconds": 84.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Alright, is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.44,
      "end_seconds": 89.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Right, uh, yes, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.74,
      "end_seconds": 93.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.97,
      "end_seconds": 98.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Codeine. I come out in... well, feeling very drowsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.62,
      "end_seconds": 113.16,
      "duration_seconds": 13.54,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.19,
      "end_seconds": 116.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.21,
      "end_seconds": 119.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.46,
      "end_seconds": 122.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Tiotropium inhaler, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.81,
      "end_seconds": 126.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.36,
      "end_seconds": 129.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "About three months now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.48,
      "end_seconds": 130.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.6,
      "end_seconds": 136.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "I'm on ramipril, 5 milligrams, every morning for my blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.37,
      "end_seconds": 140.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.87,
      "end_seconds": 153.89,
      "duration_seconds": 12.02,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.65,
      "end_seconds": 162.06,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.08,
      "end_seconds": 182.75,
      "duration_seconds": 19.67,
      "text": "Well, I have COPD, for two years. I did try to ignore it for a while. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help. I've had high blood pressure for nearly five years now. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.51,
      "end_seconds": 193.71,
      "duration_seconds": 10.2,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known high blood pressure. We'll keep that in mind today. Okay, have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.08,
      "end_seconds": 209.18,
      "duration_seconds": 15.1,
      "text": "Right, um, for the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.67,
      "end_seconds": 211.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "I'll take a few measurements first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.6,
      "end_seconds": 224.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Okay, give me a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.34,
      "end_seconds": 253.61,
      "duration_seconds": 9.27,
      "text": "Okay: respiratory rate 14, blood pressure 125 over 74, temperature 36.5, pulse is 68 beats a minute. I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.11,
      "end_seconds": 257.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.05,
      "end_seconds": 262.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Okay, let's do a quick examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.26,
      "end_seconds": 267.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Alright, turn your head to the side for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.79,
      "end_seconds": 279.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Chest sounds clear, a bit of wheeze when you breathe out hard."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.55,
      "end_seconds": 306.87,
      "duration_seconds": 22.32,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together. Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.12,
      "end_seconds": 310.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Well, okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.5,
      "end_seconds": 328.62,
      "duration_seconds": 17.12,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, my working impression is nicotine dependence. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. It could also be early chronic bronchitis, so we'll keep that open. Is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 329.44,
      "end_seconds": 339.62,
      "duration_seconds": 10.18,
      "text": "Yes, um, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.07,
      "end_seconds": 350.03,
      "duration_seconds": 8.96,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange breathing tests for smoker's cough. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 351.47,
      "end_seconds": 353.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Alright. When can I do that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.33,
      "end_seconds": 367.39,
      "duration_seconds": 12.06,
      "text": "I'll start you on nicotine patches, 14 milligrams, once a day, for six weeks. That's for smoking cessation. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.79,
      "end_seconds": 370.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Okay, and I take that after food?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.21,
      "end_seconds": 394.27,
      "duration_seconds": 20.06,
      "text": "Pick a quit date this month, and tell your family so they can back you up. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 395.74,
      "end_seconds": 399.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "I mean, you know, got it, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 400.39,
      "end_seconds": 406.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.23,
      "text": "Let's review you in four weeks. Can you run through the plan with me quickly, just to be certain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 407.4,
      "end_seconds": 411.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "So, I come back in four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 411.72,
      "end_seconds": 415.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Okay, we're done for today. Take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 415.88,
      "end_seconds": 420.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I'll get started on all of that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 421.89,
      "end_seconds": 422.76,
      "duration_seconds": 0.87,
      "text": "Alright, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}